<.shell title="Stat" current={:stat}>
  <h1>Stat</h1>
  <p class="lead">A number, what it counts, and how it compares.</p>

  <div class="chart-stats">
    <.stat value="124" label="Activities in 2025" delta="Up 12 on this time last year">
      <.sparkline values={[12, 10, 9, 11, 12, 12, 15, 17, 20, 20, 16, 4]} />
    </.stat>
    <.stat
      series={:incident}
      value="70"
      label="Incidents in 2025"
      delta="Up 1 on this time last year"
    >
      <.sparkline series={:incident} values={[5, 4, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 11, 15, 14, 9, 2]} />
    </.stat>
    <.stat value="6,289h" label="Member hours" delta="Up 875 on this time last year" />
    <.stat value="59" label="Current members" delta="8 joined in 2025" />
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>A few numbers at the top of a dashboard. One number is a stat, not a chart.</p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The label says what it counts and over when.</li>
    <li>The line under it compares with the same days last year.</li>
    <li>A sparkline shows the last 12 months. The top rule takes the series colour.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.stat value="…" label="…" delta="…"&gt;</code>, with an optional
    <code>&lt;.sparkline values=&#123;…&#125; /&gt;</code>
    inside, in a <code>.chart-stats</code>
    row. From <code>Web.Components.Chart</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
